                                ['type' => 'intro', 'title' => 'Anatomy of an argument', 'body' => 'Every argument has three parts: a claim (what the author wants you to accept), evidence (the support offered), and a warrant (the often-unstated assumption connecting them). Critical readers test all three — and the warrant is where weak arguments usually hide.'],
                                ['type' => 'explanation', 'title' => 'Five fallacies worth naming', 'body' => "Ad hominem — attacking the person instead of the argument: \"You can't trust her budget analysis; she failed math in college.\"\n\nStraw man — refuting a distorted version of the opposing view: \"They want fewer meetings, so apparently they want no communication at all.\"\n\nFalse dichotomy — pretending only two options exist: \"Either we cut staff or the company dies.\"\n\nSlippery slope — claiming one step inevitably leads to catastrophe without showing the chain: \"Allow remote work and soon nobody will ever meet again.\"\n\nHasty generalization — a big conclusion from a tiny sample: \"Two customers complained, so the launch is a disaster.\"", 'body_id' => 'Lima sesat pikir umum: ad hominem (menyerang orangnya), straw man (menyerang versi karikatur argumen), dikotomi palsu (seolah hanya ada dua pilihan), slippery slope (rantai bencana tanpa bukti), dan generalisasi tergesa-gesa (kesimpulan besar dari sampel kecil).'],
                                ['type' => 'examples', 'title' => 'Examples', 'meta' => ['items' => [
                                    ['en' => 'Claim: remote work boosts productivity. Evidence: output rose 12%. Warrant: output measures productivity.', 'id' => 'Klaim: kerja jarak jauh menaikkan produktivitas. Bukti: output naik 12%. Asumsi: output mengukur produktivitas.'],
                                    ['en' => '"Either you support this bill or you don\'t care about safety" is a false dichotomy.', 'id' => '"Dukung RUU ini atau Anda tidak peduli keselamatan" adalah dikotomi palsu.'],
                                ]]],
                                ['type' => 'vocabulary', 'title' => 'Argument terms', 'meta' => ['words' => [
                                    ['word' => 'premise', 'ipa' => '/ˈprem.ɪs/', 'meaning_id' => 'premis; dasar argumen', 'example' => 'The argument rests on a shaky premise.'],
                                    ['word' => 'flawed', 'ipa' => '/flɑːd/', 'meaning_id' => 'cacat; keliru', 'example' => 'The reasoning is flawed but persuasive.'],
                                    ['word' => 'undermine', 'ipa' => '/ˌʌn.dɚˈmaɪn/', 'meaning_id' => 'melemahkan; menggerogoti', 'example' => 'One counterexample undermines the whole claim.'],
                                ]]],
                                ['type' => 'note', 'title' => 'Fair reading first', 'body' => 'Before naming a fallacy, restate the argument in its strongest form (the "steel man"). If it still fails, your criticism will be unanswerable.', 'body_id' => 'Sebelum menuduh sesat pikir, ungkapkan dulu argumen lawan dalam bentuk terkuatnya ("steel man"). Jika tetap gagal, kritik Anda tak terbantahkan.'],
                            ],
