                                    ['type' => 'multiple_choice', 'prompt' => 'A survey of three users concludes "everyone hates the redesign". Which fallacy is this?', 'difficulty' => 'medium',
                                        'options' => [['Hasty generalization', true], ['False dichotomy', false], ['Ad hominem', false], ['Straw man', false]]],
                                    ['type' => 'true_false', 'prompt' => 'A warrant is the unstated assumption that links evidence to a claim.', 'config' => ['correct' => true]],
                                    ['type' => 'matching', 'prompt' => 'Match each fallacy to its description.', 'config' => ['pairs' => [
                                        ['left' => 'straw man', 'right' => 'attacks a distorted version of the view'], ['left' => 'false dichotomy', 'right' => 'pretends only two options exist'], ['left' => 'ad hominem', 'right' => 'attacks the person, not the argument']]]],
                                    ['type' => 'reading', 'prompt' => 'Which fallacy weakens the mayor\'s argument in the passage?', 'passage' => 'At the council meeting, the mayor dismissed the traffic study outright: "Its lead author doesn\'t even own a car — what could she possibly know about commuting?" He offered no response to the study\'s data on accident rates, which had been collected over five years.',
